WEBVTT - Operation Ghost Portal: The IT Helpdesk Mimic (English)

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
A morning email goes out to company software developers: 'Mandatory update: Please verify your credentials before noon.'

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
The email looks just like past IT updates with the official green security lock icon in the browser bar.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Here is the scammer’s secret weapon: an optical illusion. In different alphabets, some letters look completely identical to English letters.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
The scammer replaced the English letter 'o' with a foreign alphabet letter. To human eyes, both letters look identical.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:25.000
TraceXMail checks the actual computer code behind every letter, spotting the fake character instantly.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Looking deeper into the envelope, TraceXMail uncovered the hidden internet address where the message was drafted.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:02:00.000
TraceXMail mapped out the threat, discovering that 24 other senior developers had received the exact same trap.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Within three minutes, the security team blocked the fake domain company-wide.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Not a single employee password was stolen. By catching the optical illusion at the letter level, TraceXMail kept the keys safe.
